&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competition Rules and Important Considerations for Applicants&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Eligibility and Registration&lt;/strong&gt;: All team members must attend the same accredited U.S. undergraduate institution and remain enrolled there throughout the competition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Students graduating outside the December 2028–July 2030 eligibility window are not eligible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teams that do not follow the registration requirements may be disqualified.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Final Round Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All team members must be available to attend the final round in New York City on November 12–13.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Each team member must have a speaking role in the final presentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teams with absent members may be disqualified.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel and Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; Point72 will cover travel and accommodation expenses within reason.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contact Information&lt;/strong&gt;: If you have further questions, please contact us at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:AcademyRecruiting@point72.com&quot;&gt;AcademyRecruiting@point72.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Cubist:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cubist Systematic Strategies, an affiliate of Point72, deploys systematic, computer-driven trading strategies across multiple liquid asset classes, including equities, futures and foreign exchange. The core of our effort is rigorous research into a wide range of market anomalies, fueled by our unparalleled access to a wide range of publicly available data sources.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is focused on systematic equity trading. &amp;nbsp;It is established, yet still pre-trade, offering an exciting opportunity to join at an early stage and be involved in a broad range of development areas. &amp;nbsp;The team members come from a mixture of quant analyst and development backgrounds, using the combination of skills to achieve a common goal. &amp;nbsp;All team members are based in the London office five days a week to maximize communication and interaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;An ideal growth role to suit a developer looking for additional responsibilities and independence. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities may include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Building components for all aspects of live trading and research environments.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Driving automation and robustness of our processes.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Developing robust data checking and handling procedures.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Monitoring and troubleshooting any issues that should arise.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Shared responsibility for timely and correct operation of trading systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent in computer science or other STEM discipline&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;2+ years commercial experience with Python and its data science libraries on Linux.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Pragmatic balance between attention to detail and delivery focus.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ability to work with ambiguous requirements.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Self-driven, owning problems while knowing when to seek advice.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Knowledge of finance and trading systems a plus.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience with a systems programming language (e.g. C++, Rust) a plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Commercial use of cloud compute and containers a plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong analytical skills and command of statistics a plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Be in the office five days a week.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Commitment to the highest ethical standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2026 Point72 Academy Case Competition—New York City&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Point72 Academy Case Competition is your chance to showcase your investing skills by presenting a stock pitch to Point72 with a team from your university.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;You and one to three teammates will analyze a company, develop an investment thesis using publicly available sources only, and submit your pitch. Finalists will be paired with a Point72 mentor and given the opportunity to present their pitch to Point72 investment professionals in our New York City office. Prizes include scholarships and an accelerated interview process for future opportunities. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prep your pitch: &lt;/strong&gt;Research a company selected by Point72, develop your investment thesis using publicly available sources only, and bring your analysis to life in a presentation. You’re encouraged to use AI thoughtfully to support your research and analysis.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Refine with a Mentor:&lt;/strong&gt; If your team is selected as a finalist, you’ll be paired with a Point72 mentor who will provide feedback as you prepare for the final round.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Present your case: &lt;/strong&gt;Finalist teams will travel to New York City to present their investment pitch to Point72 investors. You’ll also network with your peers and representatives from our recruiting, Academy, and investing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
