&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor execution across equities, FX, Futures and other asset classes, trading in different regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide first-line support for any issues arising from the automated execution flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct project work in areas including adding new liquidity to the execution platform and reducing the cost of implementing WorldQuant’s models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze large datasets to guide further automation and refinement of execution desk processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface directly with Portfolio Managers, Brokers, Senior Management, Compliance, Risk and many other teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in a quantitative or technical discipline from a top tier institution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of work experience gained in a buy-side or sell-side institution in a Trading, DevOps or Analytics role supporting investment strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm to learn more about financial markets and execution trading&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with scripting languages (Python) and databases (SQL) a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with at least one mainstream asset class (equities, FX, fixed income, credit, derivatives)&lt;/li&gt;
